$ Oracle: Dead Connection Detection (DCD)
@ Dead Connection Detection

Dead Connection Detection (DCD) attempts to detect the unexpected loss of an Oracle connection where the client does not properly disconnect itself from the → development/databases/Oracle/architecture/session.
-
DCD can also be used to keep database connections alive accross a firewall where the firewall is configured to terminate idle connections.

DCD is enabled by setting the `→ development/databases/Oracle/Net/sqlnet_ora` parameter `sqlnet.expire_time` on the server.

With DCD, the server sends *probe packets* in the intervals specified by the `sqlnet.expire_time` value.

